# Author synchronization: canonical page context

This is author self-check evidence, not independent semantic review or canonical cutover. Only the two named authored drafts were edited. Production, canonical Markdown, schema, CLI, and CI remain root-owned. No commit was made by this author.

Input was initially fixed at HEAD 60977a4 (implementation source change 87ce544); before-0/1 are the initial source bytes, before-2 the authoring rules, before-3/4 the original drafts. Root subsequently amended only the new chapter 16 budget description while authoring was in progress. source-final-16.md and source-final-21.md preserve the final reviewed input bytes. The manifest lists both revisions rather than overwriting initial evidence.

Chapter 16 adds the sibling Section page_projection under section 3, following registry. The prior two paragraphs about actual GitHub aliases and example evaluation keep their original bytes, and now follow the new subsection as in Markdown. The entire original draft is preserved by one insertion. Six new paragraphs and an ordered four-item list reproduce 10 source units, 37 Sentences. The list preserves domain/zero byte, u64 big-endian framing and page count, registry order, six per-page fields, and source/alias SHA-256 order. Renderer and command code values remain literal InlineCode bytes. Fixed inputs, mixed legacy /2 body correspondence and old metadata, whole-set success, no ambient files, nonrecursive input identity, new-directory failure behavior, all numeric caps and shared output Budget are retained.

The final budget amendment preserves optional output_limits using the existing eight-resource OutputLimits, selection before starting, omitted default, old-only per-page behavior, no implicit increase or stop reset, actual limits and initial usage, and usage before receipt serialization. The latter excludes final serialization/output charges; it is not described as final operation usage. No benchmark numbers were added.

Chapter 21 changes only the two obsolete host-status sentences in the last paragraph. It adds an actual Relative link to 16-doc-migration.md with display 16章, assigns canonical context digest and Markdown set export to the host, preserves typed no-I/O and PageSet identity scope, and does not infer HTML/Web/publication acceptance from Markdown success. The complete resulting paragraph matches the current source, with Markdown inline-code/link notation reduced to display text.

Normal prose is manually written as one sentence literal per sentence; sentences needing code or a link use explicit sentence construction. Ruby applies only to Kanji. Readings were checked in context: 前置=ぜんち, 後付=あとづ plus け, 書込み=書込/かきこ plus み, 一つ=一/ひと plus つ, 消費済み=消費済/しょうひず plus み. Existing raw code, links and prose were not reauthored. No new translation or ornamental Anno was invented.

Validation: both full drafts pass tools.audit.structure Parser against current forms. check.py checks exact new source paragraph/list/code ordering after removing source soft wraps and Markdown decoration, final chapter 21 paragraph/link target, Kanji-only Ruby bases and unannotated Kanji absence in new prose, constrained line-diff operations, UTF-8 without BOM and LF. This structure audit is not the production parser. No native/WASI parse, lower, renderer, browser, or canonical cutover test was run by this author. Independent review remains pending.

Authoring corrections before final audit: the first list draft omitted ListItem's explicit none argument; all four entries were corrected after the structural checker rejected them. The first source-comparison run also detected root's intervening budget amendment; the manual amendment was then applied. These were author self-check failures, not production regressions. Final checks pass.
